---
import { Content as Help } from "../content/rendering.md";
---

<details id="render-settings" hidden>
  <summary>Rendering</summary>
  <div id="render-panel" class="settings-panel">
    <label>
      Preset
      <select id="render-preset">
        <option value="ultra" selected>
          Ultra
        </option>
        <option value="ps1">PS1</option>
        <option value="custom">Custom</option>
      </select>
    </label>
    <Help />
    <label>
      Scale
      <select id="render-scale" aria-label="Rendering resolution">
        <option value="0">Auto</option>
        <option value="1">1×</option>
        <option value="2">2×</option>
        <option value="3">3×</option>
        <option value="4">4×</option>
        <option value="5">5×</option>
        <option value="6">6×</option>
        <option value="7">7×</option>
        <option value="8" selected>
          8×
        </option>
      </select>
    </label>
    <p>
      Auto fits the rendering scale to the window and display pixel density. Textures retain their
      original detail.
    </p>
    <label>
      Stabilize 3D vertices <input id="subpixel-vertices" type="checkbox" checked />
    </label>
    <p>Retains fractional vertex positions to reduce polygon jitter.</p>
    <p id="network-render-note" hidden>
      Network matches render at 30 FPS without motion smoothing. Single-player timing settings are
      restored when the match ends.
    </p>
    <label>
      Motion smoothing <input id="render-smoothing" type="checkbox" checked />
    </label>
    <label class="smoothing-range">
      Smoothing delay
      <input
        id="render-smoothing-delay"
        type="range"
        min="0"
        max="7"
        step="1"
        value="7"
        aria-describedby="render-smoothing-note"
      />
    </label>
    <div id="render-smoothing-ends" aria-hidden="true">
      <span>0 ms · Prediction</span>
      <span>Full interpolation</span>
    </div>
    <output id="render-smoothing-readout" for="render-smoothing-delay">
      33.3 ms · Full interpolation · No prediction
    </output>
    <p id="render-smoothing-note">
      Lower delay makes motion respond sooner and can make corrections more visible. Contact can
      briefly add pose delay. One simulation frame is 33.3 ms at 30 TPS. Turn smoothing off for
      Vanilla motion.
    </p>
    <label>
      Perspective-correct textures <input id="perspective-textures" type="checkbox" checked />
    </label>
    <p>Reduces texture warping on 3D surfaces.</p>
    <label>
      Car LOD distance
      <select id="car-lod-distance">
        <option value="1">1× — Original</option>
        <option value="2">2×</option>
        <option value="4">4×</option>
        <option value="8" selected>
          8×
        </option>
      </select>
    </label>
    <p>Keeps detailed car models farther away. Higher values draw more polygons.</p>
    <label>
      World draw distance
      <select id="draw-distance">
        <option value="1">1× — Original</option>
        <option value="2">2×</option>
        <option value="4">4×</option>
        <option value="8" selected>
          8×
        </option>
      </select>
    </label>
    <p>Extends detailed scenery and its polygon budget. Higher values cost performance.</p>
    <label>
      Dithering
      <select id="render-dithering">
        <option value="0">Game default</option>
        <option value="1">Off</option>
      </select>
    </label>
    <p>Disabling the PS1 grain can reveal color banding.</p>
    <label>
      Render limit
      <select id="render-limit" aria-describedby="render-limit-note">
        <option value="30">30 FPS</option>
        <option value="60">60 FPS</option>
        <option value="120" selected>
          120 FPS
        </option>
        <option value="0">Display refresh rate</option>
      </select>
    </label>
    <p id="render-limit-note">
      Simulation stays at 30 TPS. Higher frame rates are available with motion smoothing and up to
      two players. Vanilla, menus and video keep their original timing.
    </p>
    <label>
      Performance graphs <input id="render-fps" type="checkbox" />
    </label>
    <p>Simulation, render and browser callback rates over the last 15 seconds.</p>
    <button id="render-reset" type="button">
      Restore defaults
    </button>
  </div>
</details>
